cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Prime Number Studies: independent re-derivations, measurements
  and negative results around the division table
message: >-
  If you use this material, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohamed
    family-names: Osman
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5912-999X'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Osman209/prime-number-studies'
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21638887
    description: Concept DOI (always resolves to the latest version)
abstract: >-
  Notes, measurements and verified code from a self-directed study
  of the multiplicative structure of the integers, starting from the
  division table. Contains independent re-derivations of known
  results (the sieve of Sundaram; the Hardy-Littlewood singular
  series; the explicit formula; Ramanujan-Fourier analysis of
  r-even functions; the Szego limit theorem; the Li-Sekatskii
  shifted Li coefficients; the major-arc expansion of the circle
  method), documented negative
  results and controls, and runnable verification scripts for every
  table and figure. No claim is made about the Riemann Hypothesis.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - prime numbers
  - sieve of Sundaram
  - divisor function
  - Hardy-Littlewood singular series
  - Riemann zeta function
  - prime gaps
  - gcd kernel
  - Toeplitz matrices
  - Szego limit theorem
  - von Mangoldt function
  - reproducible research
